  "summary": "The bauxite mine area model shows the whole mining sequence on one plateau, from undisturbed forest on the right to rehabilitated land on the left: clearing, topsoil and overburden stripping, caprock drill-and-blast, excavation of the ore down to the kaolinitic clay floor, backfill, and rehabilitation. The cut face shows the lateritic profile: topsoil, laterite overburden, ferricrete caprock, friable gibbsitic bauxite and clay. Trucks run the real-time load–haul–dump cycle from the excavators, up the 10 % box-cut ramp and along the haul road to the primary sizing station; the ROM pad holds the grade-bin blending reserve.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Mining — area overview",
    "type": "Open-cut plateau bauxite mine (strip mining with progressive rehabilitation)"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "scale": "Real size (metres); profile thicknesses typical, not a survey",
    "animation": "Real-time haul cycle (~7 min loop): excavators top-load trucks in ~6 passes, trucks haul up the ramp to the sizing station, reverse to the wheel stop and tip. Distances compressed: real one-way haul 2–8 km, real cycle ≈ 25–30 min",
    "basis": "Reference-plant design basis A01 (knowledge-based)"
  },
